pub trait MdnBackend: Send + Sync {
    // Send one or more MDNs. For each entry in send map:
    //   - Fetch the referenced email (for_email_id) to get Disposition-Notification-To, Original-Message-ID, Original-Recipient
    //   - Build and transmit the RFC 5322 MDN message
    //   - Return server-set fields (final_recipient, original_message_id, mdn_gateway, original_recipient, error) for sent entries
    //   - Return SetError for failed entries
    // on_success_update_email is forwarded to MailBackend::update_emails on full success (or partial — per-entry).
    async fn send_mdns(
        &self,
        account_id: &Id,
        identity_id: &Id,
        send: HashMap<Id, Mdn>,
    ) -> Result<MdnSendResult, BackendSetError>;

    // Parse a raw RFC 5322 blob as an MDN.
    //   - Retrieve blob bytes
    //   - Parse multipart/report with message/disposition-notification part
    //   - Correlate originalMessageId to a known Email if possible (forEmailId)
    //   - Lowercase actionMode, sendingMode, type per draft §2
    // Returns ParsedMdn for each blob: Ok(Mdn), Err(NotParsable), or Err(NotFound)
    async fn parse_mdns(
        &self,
        account_id: &Id,
        blob_ids: Vec<Id>,
    ) -> Result<MdnParseResult, BackendChangesError>;
}

MdnSendResult { sent: HashMap<Id,Mdn>, not_sent: HashMap<Id,SetError> }
MdnParseResult { parsed: HashMap<Id,Mdn>, not_parsable: Vec<Id>, not_found: Vec<Id> }

Note: the $mdnsent keyword enforcement (MUST set via onSuccessUpdateEmail) is done in the handler, not the backend. The backend only sends; the handler validates the onSuccessUpdateEmail map before calling the backend.

notes:
CORRECTION (from research phase):

1. parse_mdns return type: use Result<MdnParseResult, Self::Error> — NOT BackendChangesError (that is for /changes queries). The not_found/not_parsable split lives inside MdnParseResult, not the error type.

2. get_blob_bytes — design decision: add required method to MdnBackend itself:
   async fn get_blob_bytes(&self, account_id: &Id, blob_id: &Id) -> Result<Option<Vec<u8>>, Self::Error>;
   Rationale: keeps MDN opt-in self-contained; MemoryMdnBackend shares Arc<Mutex<Inner>> with MemoryMailBackend so it accesses inner.blobs directly. Adding to MailBackend would be a breaking change for all existing implementors.

3. Full trait outline:
   pub trait MdnBackend: Send + Sync {
       type Error: std::error::Error + Send + Sync + 'static;
       async fn get_blob_bytes(&self, account_id: &Id, blob_id: &Id) -> Result<Option<Vec<u8>>, Self::Error>;
       async fn send_mdns(&self, account_id: &Id, identity_id: &Id, send: HashMap<Id, Mdn>) -> Result<MdnSendResult, BackendSetError<Self::Error>>;
       async fn parse_mdns(&self, account_id: &Id, blob_ids: Vec<Id>) -> Result<MdnParseResult, Self::Error>;
   }

   MdnSendResult { sent: HashMap<Id, Mdn>, not_sent: HashMap<Id, SetError> }
   MdnParseResult { parsed: HashMap<Id, Mdn>, not_parsable: Vec<Id>, not_found: Vec<Id> }
